for more on the war we are joined Now by  John Kirby he is the coordinator for  strategic Communications at the National  Security Council at the White House also  retired Admiral in the U.S Navy Admiral  Kirby good morning thank you for being  here uh we we've seen strikes on  civilians uh strikes on women and  children and now we are confronting the  possibility of a deep humanitarian  crisis people freezing to death going  without water there's a perennial  question for white houses like yours is  there a line here or are we just going  to let people suffer  well we're going to continue to make  sure we're supporting Ukraine as best we  can the United States is the largest  contributor of Financial and economic  assistance for humanitarian purposes  like this to Ukraine we're also the  largest contributor of security  assistants now 17 billion dollars worth  of weapons and capabilities to allow  them to continue to defend their  territory into some and to take some of  those towns and Villages back and  they're very much in the fight right now  both in the East and the South and we're  going to do everything we can to make  sure that they can stay in that fight  we are the largest contributor and I  want to get to the money question in a  moment but is there a line or a Zone a  way of thinking where the U.S intervenes  in a deeper way than it is currently not  just money not just arms there's  obviously the president's been very  clear we're not going to put U.S troops  on the ground to fight in Ukraine uh we  are going to do everything we can as we  have now for going on eight months to  make sure that the Ukrainian armed  forces have what they need in the field  and that just isn't coming from the  United States we're also leading  literally leading and coordinating  International efforts to get additional  weapons and capabilities into their  hands sometimes in in many cases  capabilities that they know better and  can use faster than even the ones that  we're providing from our own stocks so  we're going to stay at this you've heard  the president talk about that as long as  it takes we're committed to that as long  as it takes so let's talk about the  money uh component on the subject of as  long as it takes by our count it's  nearly 100 billion dollars in Aid to  Ukraine I know we're not the only  country kicking in but at a time when  there are a lot of taxpayer needs here  is there a line for the White House  where you're not going to spend taxpayer  money there we have had great support  from both sides of the aisle in Congress  over the course of the last eight months  uh terrific support I think everybody  realizes what's at stake here which is  more than just uh you know the town of  Curson or harkiv or slovians it's really  about this idea of sovereignty and it's  really about what the security  environment in Europe is going to look  like going forward it has changed today  and and it it affects the United States  and our national security interests  because so many of our allies and  partners are now in a different security  footprint than they were before we have  20 000 more troops on the European  continent now than we did you know again  nine nine months ago eight months ago so  we are we're working this very very hard  uh and we're going to stay at it uh  Admiral the House GOP leader Kevin  McCarthy on the subject of support from  Congress he said if the Republicans take  control they're not going to write a  blank check for Ukraine uh in the new  year is he going to get a phone call  from you today this has not been about  writing blank checks for Ukraine this  has been about bipartisan support in  Congress to continue to make sure that  Ukraine can defend itself and it can  stand up for its sovereignty because  that's really what's at stake here aside  of course from the literally hundreds of  thousands of Ukrainian lives that that  have been affected by by this war so  we've had great support we're going to  continue to work hand in glove with  Congress going forward for additional  financial support for Ukraine and we're  confident that we're going to be able to  to work with them to that to that end  all right Admiral Kirby thank you very  much my pleasure
 

